    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What changed\n\nTelephone numbers are now normalized to **E.164** on create (`POST /api/owners`), stored and returned in that form, and duplicate detection compares E.164 values.\n\n**New normalization logic** \u2014 `OwnerTelephone.java` (new helper):\n- Strips spaces, dashes and brackets.\n- If a leading `+` (explicit country code) is present, keeps it as-is.\n- Otherwise assumes country code `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits.\n- Requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, else the value is rejected.\n- `toE164(...)` throws `InvalidOwnerTelephoneException` (\u2192 400); `canonical(...)` is a non-throwing variant used for comparison, falling back to digits-only for legacy data.\n\n**Wired into the pipeline:**\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 replaced the \"strip to exactly 10 digits\" rule with `OwnerTelephone.toE164(...)`, storing the E.164 string on the body.\n- `EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone` \u2014 now compares E.164 values (`OwnerTelephone.canonical`) instead of raw digit strings.\n\n**Supporting updates:**\n- `Owner` entity \u2014 the telephone `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")` + `@Digits` (which would reject an E.164 value on persist) replaced with `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")`.\n- `InvalidOwnerTelephoneException` \u2014 message updated to reflect E.164.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 telephone schema description/pattern/example updated to E.164; `VARCHAR(20)` columns already fit.\n\n## Tests\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`:\n- `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`\n- `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`\n- `12` \u2192 400 (can't form valid E.164)",
